I added `__builtin_expect` branch hints so the compiler lays out the common cached-`type` fast path and the valid-profile path as fall-through, avoiding taken-branch penalties; behaviour is unchanged.

```cpp
FIT_UINT8 Field::GetType() const
{
    if ( __builtin_expect(type != FIT_UINT8_INVALID, 1) )
        return type;

    if ( __builtin_expect((profile == NULL) || (profileIndex >= profile->numFields), 0) )
        return FIT_UINT8_INVALID;

    return profile->fields[profileIndex].type;
}
```